>> title: Berbere
>> category: Spice Blends & Marinades
>> tags: ethiopian, chiles, spice blend, toasted, pantry
>> counters: Curry House
>> aka: berbere spice, berberé
>> pairs-with: doro-wat, injera
>> servings: 20
>> time: 25 min
>> slack: narrow — the fenugreek goes bitter just after it goes brown, and there is no picking it back out of a ground powder

>> step: toast in a dry skillet 3 min
Toast @coriander seeds{2%Tbs}(12 g), @fenugreek seeds{1%tsp}, @ajwain seeds{1%tsp}, @nigella seeds{1%tsp}, @cloves{1/2%tsp}, and @green cardamom pods{1%tsp} in a dry #skillet{} over medium heat until fragrant, about ~{3%min}.

>> step: add, toast 1 min more
Add @dried red chiles{1%oz}(28 g; stemmed, seeded for less heat) to @&(~1)toasted spices{} and toast ~{1%min} more.

>> step: cool, grind fine
Cool @&(~1)mixture{} completely, then grind to a fine powder in a #spice grinder{}.

>> step: whisk in
Whisk @sweet paprika{1/4%cup}(28 g), @ground ginger{1%Tbs}, @ground cinnamon{1%tsp}, @ground allspice{1/2%tsp}, and @kosher salt{1%Tbs} into @&(~1)powder{}.
